01:18:03.380 --> 01:18:05.750
might very well be overwhelming,

01:18:05.750 --> 01:18:08.150
but it will make sense
someday if you stick with it.

01:18:08.150 --> 01:18:10.610
I promise, oh, I've added notes,

01:18:10.610 --> 01:18:13.450
but really don't let this stress you out.

01:18:13.450 --> 01:18:15.750
The reason why I'm talking
about this behavior is,

01:18:15.750 --> 01:18:17.940
because the Twilio JavaScript client

01:18:17.940 --> 01:18:19.880
works like most JavaScript libraries.

01:18:19.880 --> 01:18:21.780
It's asynchronous, and it relies on

01:18:21.780 --> 01:18:24.360
a concept called promises.

01:18:24.360 --> 01:18:26.400
So the way the promises work

01:18:26.400 --> 01:18:27.900
is that you set up handlers

01:18:27.900 --> 01:18:30.900
for when your method
call actually completes.

01:18:30.900 --> 01:18:34.150
So to get our message
log, we use this method.

01:18:34.150 --> 01:18:35.523
There's a method called,

01:18:35.523 --> 01:18:40.523
so we do client.messages.list,

01:18:41.160 --> 01:18:42.880
and what that method returns

01:18:42.880 --> 01:18:45.670
is an object that is called a promise.

01:18:45.670 --> 01:18:47.617
It's a promise of a future value.

01:18:47.617 --> 01:18:50.994
The future value in this
case will be our messages.

01:18:50.994 --> 01:18:54.310
So promises have an
important method on them,

01:18:54.310 --> 01:18:56.420
and it's called then.

01:18:56.420 --> 01:18:59.330
So I'm gonna go ahead,
and chain on that message.

01:18:59.330 --> 01:19:04.330
I'll say .then, and this method
should be given a function

01:19:05.290 --> 01:19:07.610
that accepts of value.

01:19:07.610 --> 01:19:09.180
So I'm gonna pass it a function.

01:19:09.180 --> 01:19:10.980
Now in modern JavaScript

01:19:10.980 --> 01:19:13.640
you can use what are known
as fat arrow functions.

01:19:13.640 --> 01:19:15.807
So what I'll do is I'll
put the name of the value,

01:19:15.807 --> 01:19:19.112
and the value here is messages, right?

01:19:19.112 --> 01:19:20.720
Because this is what I'm
expecting to be returned,

01:19:20.720 --> 01:19:21.790
and then I'm gonna put a fat arrow,

01:19:21.790 --> 01:19:23.740
which is an equal sign of greater than,

01:19:25.000 --> 01:19:26.530
and then I'm gonna put the function body.

01:19:26.530 --> 01:19:29.853
So let's just log out
the most recent message.

01:19:32.680 --> 01:19:34.293
Okay, so we'll do a console.log,

01:19:35.480 --> 01:19:37.100
and I'm gonna use back ticks

01:19:37.100 --> 01:19:42.100
so that we can get a string interpolation,

01:19:42.410 --> 01:19:45.590
and I want it to be the
first one in the array.

01:19:45.590 --> 01:19:47.207
So we're gonna say

01:19:47.207 --> 01:19:52.207
the most recent message is dollar sign,

01:19:55.160 --> 01:19:59.980
curly brace messages, zero,
because it's in array.body,

